<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Web">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <OutputType>Library</OutputType>
    <Authors>Fred Catellier-Poulin, Michael Jolin, Claudine Gagnon</Authors>
    <Company>CAUCA 9-1-1</Company>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/CAUCA-9-1-1/cause-security-management</RepositoryUrl>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/CAUCA-9-1-1/cause-security-management</PackageProjectUrl>
    <GeneratePackageOnBuild>true</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
    <Description>ASP.NET Core HTTP integration (controllers, authentication, authorization) for Cause.SecurityManagement.Core.</Description>
    <Copyright>CAUCA 9-1-1 (c) 2025</Copyright>
    <PackageTags>Cause Security Management AspNetCore Http Controllers Cauca</PackageTags>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
10.9.0 — Adds the user edition endpoints, with a breaking change to the UserForEdition wire contract.

UserForEdition's shape changed incompatibly: the flat properties are replaced by two nested
records, Login (UserName, Password, PasswordConfirmation, TwoFactorAuthenticatorEnabled) and
PersonalInformation (FirstName, LastName, Email, PhoneNumber). Id's default also moved from
Guid.NewGuid() to Guid.Empty, since Guid.Empty is now the signal BaseUserEditionController
uses to distinguish creation from update. Any consumer serializing or constructing
UserForEdition by its old flat properties must update to the nested shape.

Adds BaseUserEditionController&lt;TUser, TUserForEdition&gt;, an abstract create/read/update endpoint
for a user's edition form, plus IUserNameAvailabilityReader /
UserNameAvailabilityReader&lt;TUser&gt; for the accompanying user-name-availability check. The save
endpoint now runs CanEditUserAsync unconditionally, including on creation — a host relying on
the previous behavior (creation open to every authenticated caller) must opt back in explicitly
in its own override. The save endpoint also gates group membership changes through the new
abstract CanGrantGroupsAsync, validates the request body through an injected
IValidator&lt;TUserForEdition&gt;, and returns the new user's identifier on a successful
creation (200) rather than 204.

All published packages must be upgraded together. See the README section on the user edition
controller for the abstract members a host must implement and the DI registrations it must add.
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
    <Version>10.9.0</Version>
    <AssemblyVersion>10.9.0</AssemblyVersion>
    <FileVersion>10.9.0</FileVersion>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>True</GenerateDocumentationFile>
